{"type": "thinking", "text": "Need verify Date gaps results.\n\n1) 1981-02-14 18:32:00 to 2026-05-03 14:49:09.\n\nCompute. From 1981-02-14 18:32:00 to 2026-02-14 18:32:00 = 45 years. Are there leap days? Number of days: years 1981..2025 = 45 years. Leap years in [1981,2025]: 1984,88,92,96,2000,04,08,12,16,20,24 = 11 leap days. So 45*365+11 = 16425+11 = 16436 days. Then from 2026-02-14 18:32 to 2026-05-03 14:49:09. Feb 14 → May 3: Feb remaining 14 days (to Feb 28) = 14 days to Feb 28? Let's compute: Feb 14 18:32 → Mar 14 18:32 = 28 days (2026 not leap). Mar 14 → Apr 14 = 31 days; Apr 14 → May 3 = 19 days. Total 78 days minus 3h42m51s: May 3 14:49:09 vs May 3 18:32:00 = 3h42m51s less. So total = 45y 2mo (Feb 14 to Apr 14) + 19d? Wait 45 years to Feb 14 2026, then +2 months = Apr 14, then 18 days 20h17m9s to May 3 14:49:09? Apr 14 18:32 → Apr 30 18:32 = 16 days; Apr 30 → May 3 14:49:09 = 2 days 20:17:09. Total 18d 20h17m9s. Yes matches \"45 y 2 mo 18 d 20 h 17 min 9 s\". Good.\n\n2) 2020-03-10 22:15:00 to 2024-08-25 09:40:30: 4 years to 2024-03-10 22:15, then 5 months to 2024-08-10 22:15, then 14 days 11h25m30s to Aug 25 09:40:30 (Aug 10 22:15 → Aug 24 22:15 = 14 days; Aug 24 22:15 → Aug 25 09:40:30 = 11:25:30). Matches.\n\n3) date(2024,1,1) to date(2024,1,8) = 1 wk. Good.\n\nNote first row's result element is TextView separate; layout odd. Fine.\n\nNow Time differences."}
