{"type": "thinking", "text": "\"-1 wk\" correct.\n\nNow test time difference with seconds: \"datetimeZ(2024,1,1,10,0,0,\\\"UTC\\\") to datetimeZ(2024,1,1,10,0,1,\\\"UTC\\\")\" → 1 s. And negative -1 s.\n\nMaybe more interesting: \"-1 d -0 h -0 min -30 s\"? Could expose \"-0\" components. Let's test \"datetimeZ(2024,1,1,10,0,0,\\\"UTC\\\") to datetimeZ(2024,1,1,9,59,30,\\\"UTC\\\")\" = -30 s. If formatter outputs \"-30 s\" fine.\n\nWhat about -1h30s = -1 h -0 min -30 s? If it omits zero minutes, \"-1 h -30 s\". Probably fine.\n\nHmm. Maybe the time difference formatter bug is with polarity *per component* applied to the absolute component values, which is correct. But what if the result has a negative sign but one component rounds to zero? Not likely.\n\nLet's think about \"normalised component formatted independently, together with its polarity\". Could produce wrong output when the normalized component is, say, -1 day but the total is positive? Impossible.\n\nMaybe the bug is in Date gaps file row 1's *result layout*: the result appears as an overlay in the input text (\"45 y 2 mo 18 d 20 h 17 min 9 s\" at position (922,371)) and the EditText also at (415,371), while row 1 has no separate result View (element [2] is View, [3] is TextView overlapping). Compare row 2: EditText at (415,649) and result TextView at (922,649). Row 1's long expression makes the row wrap? The result might be positioned below/overlapping. Not a bug per se.\n\nMaybe test Date gaps with \"datetime\" differences where sub-second? Not needed.\n\nLet's now focus on precision tests: set to 0 and verify all result lines; then toggle off; then rotate; then restore 2.\n\nPotential bug in precision: \"chosen decimal places are now applied to every result line\" — maybe percentage lines don't respect it, or temp sums don't, or the Date gaps don't. We saw temp sums and expenses respect 4. Need to check Remainders/Percentages with 4dp. Let's do that.\n\nCurrent precision is 4. Go to home, open Remainders. But scratchpad changes not saved; close it (more options? just back twice). Actually scratchpad is temporary; leave it via Back. Then check files.\n\nAlso note: precision is a global setting; changing it affects results. We need to restore to 2 at end.\n\nLet's close scratchpad and check Remainders/Percentages at 4dp."}
