{"type": "thinking", "text": "\"-1 d -1 s\" good.\n\nThe time difference formatter seems fine. Maybe the bug is with *positive* durations when weeks are introduced and there are hours but no days: e.g., 8 days → \"1 wk 1 d\". Fine.\n\nWhat if duration is exactly 28 days → \"4 wk\". fine.\n\nWhat if duration is negative and week/day components: \"-1 wk -1 d\"? Could test 8 days reversed but not needed.\n\nHmm, perhaps the time difference bug is something else: it might fail when the difference is a negative duration where the *absolute value components* should be positive after a borrow. Let's test the known problematic case: datetimeZ(2024,1,1,6,30) to datetimeZ(2024,1,1,10,0) positive 3h30m. Fine.\n\nWait—maybe the change note refers to formatting of *date/time query results* like \"hours since datetime(...)\" which show decimals. The area \"dates and times\" maybe includes those. But not in preconditions.\n\nLet me look at the changelog 4.9.4: \"Added support for sub-day time unit queries ( hours since , minutes since , seconds since , etc.) and decimal precision for date/time queries\". Hmm, result precision \"chosen decimal places applied to every result line\" may affect these queries. Not in files though.\n\nMaybe I should test additional date/time operations: \"days between date(2024,1,1) and date(2024,1,8)\"? The app uses \"to\". Fine.\n\nCould test date arithmetic with \"date(2024,1,1) + 7 days\" etc. Not in the changed areas.\n\nGiven the areas: dates and times. There may be a bug in the Date gaps file itself that we haven't noticed. Let's verify the first result again very carefully. It shows \"45 y 2 mo 18 d 20 h 17 min 9 s\" for 1981-02-14 18:32:00 → 2026-05-03 14:49:09. Wait, is the day count correct given month lengths? 2026-02-14 18:32 + 2 months = 2026-04-14 18:32. +18 days = 2026-05-02 18:32. +20h17m9s = 2026-05-03 14:49:09. Correct.\n\nSecond 2020-03-10 22:15 → 2024-08-25 09:40:30. +4y = 2024-03-10 22:15. +5mo = 2024-08-10 22:15. +14d = 2024-08-24 22:15. +11h25m30s = 2024-08-25 09:40:30. Correct.\n\nThird 1 week. Correct.\n\nNow Date gaps using \"to\" - if 'in' and 'to' same parser rule, maybe \"date(...) in date(...)\" also gives a gap. Not required.\n\nMaybe the date/time bug is in Time differences if the *seconds* component has an issue with negative zero; we tested -30s, -1d1s. Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug is \"Time difference formatter: each normalised component is now formatted independently, together with its polarity\" causing \"-4 wk -1 d -23 h\" instead of \"-4 wk 1 d 23 h\"? Same debate as before. The dev might consider per-component sign correct.\n\nLet me try to find app documentation in Help (maybe FAQ) that shows expected outputs for time differences and temperature arithmetic. Help menu in scratchpad / Settings > Help & feedback > Docs. Let's check Help & feedback. It might link to docs that describe date/time and temperature semantics. But internet? Maybe in-app help screen.\n\nLet's open Settings > Help & feedback."}
